Subject: media: i2c: vd55g1: register as a sensor subdevice

Use v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor() so the V4L2 core looks up the
sensor's privacy LED (and other sensor fwnode properties) and turns it on
while streaming. On the Surface Pro 12 (Intel) the IR camera's INT3472
provides a "privacy" LED next to the camera cluster that otherwise stayed
off while the IR camera streamed.
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g1.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g1.c
@@ -2378,7 +2378,7 @@ static int vd55g1_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 		goto err_power_off;
 	}
 
-	ret = v4l2_async_register_subdev(&sensor->sd);
+	ret = v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor(&sensor->sd);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "async subdev register failed %d\n", ret);
 		goto err_subdev;
